## Main Goal
This code calculates the **minimum number of jumps** required to reach a target distance `d`, given two possible jump lengths `a` and `b`. The algorithm assumes a frog (or similar entity) can jump either `a` or `b` units at a time, and it determines the fewest jumps needed to land exactly on or beyond position `d`, following a greedy/case-based logic rather than dynamic programming.

